# file module

The `file` module maps an input file into memory for zero-copy reads.

## Type

### `MappedFile`

A file mapped into memory.

Fields:

- `data`: `[]const u8`
- `size`: `usize`
- `map`: optional memory map handle

Nested error set:

- `OpenError`: `FileTooBig`, `FileNotFound`, `AccessDenied`, `OutOfMemory`, `SystemResources`, `Unexpected`.

Methods:

- `open(io, file_path)`: open and map a file. Empty files return an empty slice with no mapping.
- `deinit(self, io)`: unmap the file and clear the slice. Safe to call when no mapping exists.

## Example

```zig
var mapped = try sibl.MappedFile.open(io, "hello.o");
defer mapped.deinit(io);

if (mapped.data.len >= 4 and std.mem.eql(u8, mapped.data[0..4], &sibl.elf.MAGIC)) {
    // parse as ELF
}
```

## Notes

- Both absolute and relative paths work.
- Close the file handle inside `open`; the mapping stays valid.
- Call `deinit` before the mapping goes out of scope.
